          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q. Write the perimeters of the figures below in terms of straight and diagonal units.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.142,
            0.723,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. The perimeters of the figures: 8s + 2d, 4s + 6d, 12s + 6d, 18s + 6d."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.171,
            0.883,
            0.227
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q. Find various objects from your surroundings that have regular shapes and find their perimeters. Also, generalise your understanding for the perimeter of other regular polygons.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.235,
            0.822,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans. In general perimeter of regular polygons = Number of sides × Length of a side."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.289,
            0.219,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
